{"html":"<p>Your book API works: anyone can list, add and delete books. Probably not what you want in production. Spring Security protects it, and this guide builds on the API from <a href=\"/blog/essentials/build-a-rest-api-with-spring-boot/\">Build a REST API With Spring Boot</a>: reading stays public, adding needs a login, and deleting needs an admin.</p>\n<h2 id=\"two-questions-who-and-what\">Two Questions: Who and What</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Authentication:</strong> who are you? Proving identity, with a password or a token.</li>\n<li><strong>Authorization:</strong> what may you do? Checking permissions, usually by role.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A wrong password gets <strong>401 Unauthorized</strong> (despite the name, it means &quot;not authenticated&quot;). A known user without permission gets <strong>403 Forbidden</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"add-spring-security\">Add Spring Security</h2>\n<p>Add the starter to <code>pom.xml</code>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">dependency</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">groupId</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>org.springframework.boot&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">groupId</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">artifactId</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>spring-boot-starter-security&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">artifactId</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">dependency</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>The moment it&#39;s there, <strong>every</strong> endpoint requires a login, and Spring prints a generated password at startup. Secure by default; now let&#39;s open what should be open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-securityfilterchain\">The SecurityFilterChain</h2>\n<p>Rules live in a <code>SecurityFilterChain</code> bean. Each request passes through Spring Security&#39;s filters before reaching your controller:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Configuration</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">public</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> class</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> SecurityConfig</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Bean</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> SecurityFilterChain </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">securityFilterChain</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(HttpSecurity </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">http</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">throws</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Exception {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        http</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">            .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">authorizeHttpRequests</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(auth </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> auth</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">                .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">requestMatchers</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(HttpMethod.GET, </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"/api/books/**\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">permitAll</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">                .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">requestMatchers</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(HttpMethod.DELETE, </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"/api/books/**\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">hasRole</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"ADMIN\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">                .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">anyRequest</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">authenticated</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">())</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">            .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">httpBasic</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">withDefaults</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">())</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">            .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">csrf</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(csrf </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> csrf.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">disable</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">())</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">            .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">sessionManagement</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(session </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">                session.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">sessionCreationPolicy</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> http.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">build</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Reading it top to bottom:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>GET /api/books/**</code> is open to everyone.</li>\n<li><code>DELETE</code> needs the <code>ADMIN</code> role.</li>\n<li>Everything else needs any logged-in user.</li>\n<li>Rules are checked <strong>in order</strong>, first match wins, so put specific rules before general ones, and end with a catch-all.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"users-and-passwords\">Users and Passwords</h2>\n<p>For a first version, keep users in memory:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Bean</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">public</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> PasswordEncoder </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">passwordEncoder</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> PasswordEncoderFactories.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">createDelegatingPasswordEncoder</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Bean</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">public</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> UserDetailsService </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">users</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(PasswordEncoder encoder) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    return</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> InMemoryUserDetailsManager</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        User.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">withUsername</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">password</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(encoder.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">encode</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"secret\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">roles</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"USER\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">build</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(),</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        User.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">withUsername</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"admin\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">password</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(encoder.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">encode</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"admin-secret\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">roles</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"USER\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"ADMIN\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">build</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Never store passwords as plain text. The delegating encoder hashes them with <strong>bcrypt</strong> by default: a slow, salted hash, so a stolen database doesn&#39;t reveal the passwords. In a real app, <code>UserDetailsService</code> loads users from your database instead.</p>\n<h2 id=\"http-basic-stateless-and-csrf\">HTTP Basic, Stateless and CSRF</h2>\n<p><strong>HTTP Basic</strong> sends the username and password with every request, in an <code>Authorization</code> header:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">curl</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> -u</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> ana:secret</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> -X</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> POST</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> localhost:8080/api/books</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">  -H</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"Content-Type: application/json\"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">  -d</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> '{\"title\": \"Dune\", \"author\": \"Frank Herbert\", \"pages\": 412}'</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>It&#39;s simple and fine for internal tools, but only over <strong>HTTPS</strong>: the credentials are only encoded, not encrypted.</p>\n<p><strong>Stateless</strong> means Spring doesn&#39;t create a session: every request proves who it is. That suits APIs called by other programs and scales across servers.</p>\n<p><strong>CSRF</strong> protection stops other websites from making a logged-in browser send requests with its cookies. A stateless API that doesn&#39;t use cookies for login isn&#39;t exposed to that attack, so it&#39;s commonly disabled there. <strong>Keep it on</strong> if your API authenticates with session cookies, like a classic web app.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tokens-jwt\">Tokens: JWT</h2>\n<p>Sending a password on every request isn&#39;t ideal for real users. The usual approach for APIs:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The user logs in once with an identity provider, like Keycloak, Auth0, Okta or your own login service.</li>\n<li>They receive a signed <strong>JWT</strong> (JSON Web Token) that says who they are and expires soon.</li>\n<li>They send it with each request: <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code>.</li>\n<li>Your API checks the signature and expiry, without calling anyone.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Spring Security does the checking as an <strong>OAuth2 resource server</strong>: add <code>spring-boot-starter-oauth2-resource-server</code>, set <code>spring.security.oauth2.resourceserver.jwt.issuer-uri</code> to your provider, and replace <code>httpBasic</code> with <code>oauth2ResourceServer(oauth2 -&gt; oauth2.jwt(withDefaults()))</code>. The authorization rules stay the same.</p>\n<p>Avoid writing your own token signing and checking: it&#39;s easy to get subtly wrong.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing-security\">Testing Security</h2>\n<p>In Spring Boot 4, add the security test starter:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">dependency</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">groupId</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>org.springframework.boot&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">groupId</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">artifactId</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>spring-boot-starter-security-test&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">artifactId</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">scope</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>test&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">scope</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">dependency</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Without it, MockMvc tests still go through the security filters, but <code>@WithMockUser</code> has no effect, so every request is anonymous.</p>\n<p>Then test each rule, both allowed and refused:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Test</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">void</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> writingNeedsALogin</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() throws Exception {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    mockMvc.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">perform</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">post</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"/api/books\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">contentType</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">content</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(json))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">andExpect</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">status</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">isUnauthorized</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    mockMvc.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">perform</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">post</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"/api/books\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">with</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">httpBasic</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"secret\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">            .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">contentType</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">content</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(json))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">andExpect</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">status</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">isCreated</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Test</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">WithMockUser</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">roles</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"USER\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">void</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> deletingNeedsTheAdminRole</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() throws Exception {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    mockMvc.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">perform</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">delete</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"/api/books/1\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">andExpect</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">status</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">isForbidden</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>@WithMockUser</code> pretends a user is logged in, so tests can focus on authorization.</p>\n<h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common Mistakes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>permitAll()</code> too early:</strong> a broad rule like <code>/api/**</code> placed first opens everything after it.</li>\n<li><strong>Plain-text passwords</strong> or a fast hash like MD5 or SHA-256 alone: use bcrypt or another password hash.</li>\n<li><strong>Disabling CSRF</strong> in a cookie-based web app.</li>\n<li><strong>Secrets in code:</strong> read keys and passwords from environment variables or a secret manager.</li>\n<li><strong>Only testing the happy path:</strong> test that the wrong user is refused, too.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Authentication checks who you are (401 if not); authorization checks what you may do (403 if not).</li>\n<li>Adding Spring Security locks everything; open and protect endpoints in a <code>SecurityFilterChain</code>, specific rules first.</li>\n<li>Hash passwords with the delegating encoder (bcrypt), and load users with a <code>UserDetailsService</code>.</li>\n<li>Stateless APIs use HTTP Basic over HTTPS, or better, JWTs checked as an OAuth2 resource server.</li>\n<li>In Spring Boot 4, add <code>spring-boot-starter-security-test</code>, and test allowed and refused requests.</li>\n</ol>\n"}